# Cloudflare Pages and Netlify read this file from the site root.
#
# The two headers make the page cross-origin isolated, which lets the app
# use the fastest browser storage. Without them it still runs, on a slower
# storage path shown in Settings. See HOSTING.md.
# A site whose users connect Google Drive needs Google's sign-in popup to
# talk back to the page, which same-origin forbids: use
# same-origin-allow-popups there and accept the slower storage.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
# The entry files are revalidated on every load, so a replaced bundle is
# picked up at once.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/flutter_bootstrap.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/main.dart.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
